# Scope template-sync to infrastructure only.
#
# Downstream repos own their app code outright — src/, package.json, docs,
# README, configs, everything. This file makes template-sync touch nothing
# but CI pipelines, Docker, and the nginx reverse proxy, so a sync run can
# never silently clobber a downstream repo's own code.
#
# This file lives in the TEMPLATE repo only — actions-template-sync reads it
# from the source side, not the target. A copy inside a downstream repo is a
# no-op (unsupported by the action) and gets overwritten back to match this
# one on every sync anyway.
#
# Syntax: exclude everything by default (`*`), then re-include the specific
# infra paths via git pathspec negation (`:!`). See
# https://github.com/AndreasAugustin/actions-template-sync#ignore-files-and-folders-while-syncing
*

# CI pipelines (workflows + dependabot config)
:!.github
:!.github/**

# Docker
:!Dockerfile
:!.dockerignore

# Reverse proxy
:!nginx.conf
